## Score it against the spec

```bash
rungrad score ./{{.Name}} \
  --read        "widget list" \
  --mutate      "widget create demo" \
  --destructive "widget delete alpha" \
  --update
```

The product scaffold implements read output, a mutating dry-run, a safe
destructive command, endpoint resolution, manifest metadata, and an offline
update, so those rules score. It intentionally omits the auth,
name-resolution, missing-resource, backend-error, forbidden, rate-limit, and
credential-secret fixtures, which the scorer reports as not-applicable rather
than failures.

> The generated `update` command uses an offline fixed fetcher so the project can
> be scored locally without network access. Before distributing real releases,
> replace it with `update.GitHubFetcher{Owner: "{{.ReleaseOwner}}", Repo:
> "{{.ReleaseRepo}}"}` or equivalent release wiring.
